^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-03-20 15:17] observe — package-owned cli owns most commands, but spwq remains root-owned and selector traversal misses obvious references in .spw/workspace.spw.
 >>[2026-03-20 15:17] decide — treat selector correctness as the dependency edge; absorb spwq only after the seed walker becomes truthful.
 >>[2026-03-20 15:17] taste — the public command surface currently reveals internal migration seams; the goal is one canon CLI with deliberate compatibility aliases.
 >>[2026-03-20 15:17] hygiene — branch is clean on main@edd98d148ced7abefc25fa7c857544264d49195a; no unrelated drift to split.
 >>[2026-03-20 16:06] observe — repairing getNodeChildren exposed the real corpus again; pathRefs and navigable selectors now hit workspace/index manifests instead of collapsing to zero.
 >>[2026-03-20 16:06] revise — presets needed explicit node-type filters so pathRefs no longer absorb generic ~ operations and refs stay distinct from broader navigable matches.
 >>[2026-03-20 16:06] decide — normalize names around three query surfaces: query for corpus rows, select for single-file AST selection, ls for liminal sequence scanning; keep spwq and spw:seq as compatibility wrappers.
 >>[2026-03-20 16:06] surprise — LSP references regressed on performance once selector traversal became truthful; switching the adapter back to regex-first ref scanning restored 22/0 smoke without undoing CLI selector dogfooding.
 >>[2026-03-20 16:06] taste — the canonical docs were also stale on command ownership and selector count; updating them is part of the rename, not optional polish.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:35] observe — consumer repositories interact with Spw primarily through CLI. The command taxonomy must be stable enough for repo-local agent instructions and package scripts to reference without breakage.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:36] decide — resolve alias-fate: spwq should become a hidden internal wrapper (not public). External codebases should learn `spw query` and `spw select` from the start. Compatibility alias remains in workbench for migration but is not exported to site installs.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:37] decide — resolve bin-dx: document the root `spw` binary direction now in .spw/conventions/cli.spw, but defer package wiring to spw-site-install.
 >>[2026-03-27 09:13] revise — mounted consumers resolve the CLI from .spw/_workbench/packages/spw-cli/ or through a consumer-owned wrapper.
 >>[2026-03-27 13:17] decide — this branch owns verb truth, not install plumbing. Treat CLI taxonomy as a parallel substrate for site-install and release docs: this branch stabilizes names, the ecology branches teach sites how to invoke them.
 >>[2026-07-20 15:18] revise — extend verb truth into observability: roots, doctor, capabilities, and review must expose normalized evidence before LSP/editor audits can be repeatable.
}

